// OPTIONAL override — most developers do not need this file.
//
// The shared Apple Developer Team ID is already committed in Config.xcconfig,
// so the project signs and builds without any setup. For the simulator this
// file is never needed at all.
//
// You need it when you deploy to a real iPhone and Apple Watch with your own
// Apple ID. Copy this file and fill in BOTH values:
//
//   cp Local.xcconfig.template Local.xcconfig
//
// Local.xcconfig is git-ignored, so your override stays local.
DEV_TEAM_ID =

// Your own base bundle identifier. Needed together with your own team,
// because org.iremia.app is registered to the team above and cannot be
// claimed by a different one. The watch app derives its own identifier
// ($(APP_BUNDLE_ID).watchkitapp) and its companion reference from this
// value, so this single line covers both targets.
//
// Keep the line commented out unless you actually set an identifier — an
// empty value here would override the working default from Config.xcconfig
// and leave the watch app with a broken bundle identifier.
//APP_BUNDLE_ID = de.example.iremia
